# Build the agent

The plan lives in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`. Find the first unchecked task, do only that
task, tick its box, and say what you did. At a STOP, stop: summarise what the human must
review and wait for them.

## Before any task

1. Read `AGENTS.md` (rules, layout, commands) and `docs/AGENT_SPEC.md` (what to build).
2. Run `uv run pytest`. It must pass before you change anything; if it does not, report it.
3. Run `armature plan` to see open tasks and whether `armature.yaml` has unapplied changes.

## T1 Design

- Fill the Purpose, Returns and Errors lines for every tool in `docs/TOOL_CONTRACTS.md`. If a
  tool's side-effect class or arguments look wrong, change `armature.yaml` (not the generated
  code) and run `armature generate`.
- Fill the Design section of `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`: prompt outline, guardrails for every
  prohibited action in the spec, and the context policy.
- Do not write tool code yet.

## T2 Benchmark, then STOP

Use the `build-benchmark` skill. The benchmark defines "good" before any code exists, so the
agent cannot be built to the test. End the task with `armature eval validate` clean, then stop
and ask the human to verify the cases, set targets and gates, and add held-out cases.

## T3 Freeze

Only after the human approves: `armature eval freeze`. From here on, cases and graders are
read-only for you.

## T4 Build

- Implement each tool with the `add-tool` skill, one at a time, each with a unit test in
  `tests/test_tools.py` (or a new test file).
- Write `src/{{package}}/prompts/system.md` from the Design section. Keep instructions general;
  never mention a specific eval case.
- Update `docs/BUILD_STATUS.md` as each piece becomes real.
- Smoke-run `armature eval run --sample 10`.

## T5 Baseline

Run the full dev suite live (needs `{{model.api_key_env}}`). Log it as run #1 in
`evals/EXPERIMENTS.md` with the run id, scores, cost and latency.

## T6 Optimize

Use the `optimize-agent` skill until the targets in `evals/BENCHMARK.md` are met.

## T7 Verify

`armature eval run --suite heldout`. If held-out trails dev by more than the gap in the plan,
the agent is overfitting the dev cases: go back to T6 and make more general fixes.

## T8 Report

Write `evals/EVAL_REPORT.md`: dev vs held-out, per-dimension and per-category results, cost
and latency, remaining failures with run ids, and suggested new cases.

## When something breaks

Use the `debug-run` skill. Never weaken a test, a limit or a grader to get past a failure.
